---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { readData, type Coverage } from '../lib/data';
const cov = readData<Coverage & Record<string, any>>('coverage.json');
const REPO = 'https://github.com/motmar16/harta-criminali-in-serie';
---
<Base title="About, methodology and sources — Serial Killer Map"
      description="How the map is built: sources, inclusion rules, location method, limits and corrections.">
  <PageHeader />
  <main class="page prose">
    <h1>About this map</h1>
    <p>A documentary map of serial killers, spree killers and mass murderers worldwide, built only from public sources,
      with the source of every fact shown on each record. It is not sensational content: there are no rankings, and
      no photographs of victims. Victims are named only when the linked Wikipedia article already names them.</p>
    <p class="muted">{cov.killers_total.toLocaleString('en')} records · data updated {cov.generated_at}.</p>

    <h2>Who is included</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Wikidata</strong>: people whose occupation is serial killer, spree killer, mass murderer or school shooter.</li>
      <li><strong>Wikipedia</strong> (English): the lists of serial killers and the “Serial killers” and “Mass murderers”
        category trees. Military and state violence (war crimes, genocide) is excluded.</li>
      <li><strong>Murderpedia</strong>: profiles classified “Serial killer”, “Spree killer” or “Mass murderer”.
        Only structured facts are used, never its texts or photographs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each record shows a legal status. <em>Suspected / alleged</em> people and <em>unidentified</em> perpetrators are
      marked as such and are not presented as convicted. Unidentified perpetrators have no known sex and no photo.</p>

    <h2>Where the dots are</h2>
    <p>A dot marks the <strong>area where the crimes took place</strong>, not the place of birth or imprisonment. In order of
      preference it comes from: manual corrections, the Wikipedia infobox, the location of the linked event on Wikidata
      (for example a massacre), Radford University timelines, places linked in sentences about the crimes (in any
      language), the Murderpedia “Location” field, and finally the country only. Large, faded dots mean the location is
      only known at state or country level. Individual crime scenes are not mapped yet.</p>

    <h2>Sources and licences</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Wikidata — CC0.</li>
      <li>Wikipedia — summaries quoted under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>,
        with a link to the exact revision.</li>
      <li>Murderpedia — structured facts only (classification, method, location), with a link to each profile.</li>
      <li>Radford University, Psychology 405 “Serial Killer Timelines” — link to each timeline (PDF); only places are extracted.</li>
      <li>Portraits — Wikimedia Commons only, with free licences checked file by file; author and licence under each image.</li>
      <li>Map — © OpenStreetMap contributors, tiles by OpenFreeMap.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Errors and corrections</h2>
    <p>Data compiled automatically will contain mistakes. Please report them, ideally with a source:
      <a href={`${REPO}/issues/new`}>open an issue on GitHub</a>. Requests to remove a record about a living person
      who was not convicted are handled with priority.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Source code and extracted data: <a href={REPO}>{REPO}</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 12px 16px 56px; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: 34px; margin: 10px 0 8px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 28px 0 6px; }
  .prose p, .prose li { font-size: 15.5px; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .small { font-size: 13px; }
</style>
